# Line-ending pins for executable text. On a Windows clone with Git's default
# core.autocrlf=true, checkout rewrites LF to CRLF: a CRLF shebang breaks the
# interpreter ("/usr/bin/env bash\r": no such file), and CRLF inside the guard
# hooks' embedded python heredocs would corrupt the byte-identical parser
# region that scripts/test_guardlib.py pins. Pin LF at the repo layer so every
# clone — and every project seeded from this template — checks out runnable
# scripts regardless of the machine's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
